## One thing I could not fix from data, reported rather than worked around
The derived `auto:CHECKSTANDS` rect leaves the checkout-lane slivers walkable: its bridging disconnects the whole SW quadrant in the sealed grid, which aisle-badge protection then keeps wholesale, lanes included. Every tighter seal rect I tried (left bank only, right bank only, both, bridges 14‑26) sealed the lanes but also killed the ~1800-cell post-checkout strip in front of the Business Center — real customer floor. I left the derived zone alone (`seal_zones: derived`); the one lane cell that *is* sealed, at (649,580), is in `must_not`. `far_snaps` for ENTRANCE/EXIT and PHARMACY DRIVE-THRU are the exterior door/lane labels printed outside the sales-floor boundary; SEAFOOD's new 2.8 m snap is the label moving to the customer side of its counter.

